<Layout title="Privacy | RIPL Wealth" description="How the RIPL website handles contact requests and wealth persona assessment information.">
<section class="hero"><div class="wrap article"><h1>Privacy</h1><p class="small">Website draft · Updated October 9, 2026</p><h2>Questions and contact requests</h2><p>When you submit a contact request, we collect the information you provide so Adam Kasick and Chase Bellefeuille can respond. Do not submit sensitive account details, passwords, Social Security numbers, or financial documents through these forms.</p><h2>Wealth persona assessment</h2><p>Your assessment answers are processed in your browser to generate an educational persona. Answers are not sent to analytics. If you choose to send your result to our team, your name, email, optional phone number, persona, audience track, mindset, tendency and overlapping mindsets are delivered through FormSubmit to Adam and Chase. Raw question responses are not included.</p><p>Submitting your result asks the team to contact you. It does not enroll you in an automated newsletter or request that you be contacted by text message.</p><h2>Compound-interest calculator</h2><p>Calculator inputs and results are processed in your browser. They are not submitted to RIPL or used to create a financial plan.</p><h2>Third-party services</h2><p>FormSubmit processes submitted contact information and result notifications. Calendly handles scheduling when you follow a booking link. Google Fonts supplies website fonts. Each service has its own privacy practices.</p><h2>Questions about your information</h2><p>Contact <a href="mailto:hello@riplwealth.com">hello@riplwealth.com</a> to ask about information you have provided or request that we stop contacting you.</p><p>This website privacy summary supplements the firm’s privacy notice, which is available on request. It requires firm review before public launch.</p></div></section>
</Layout>
